# The largest number of the format not above a 2-limb x: x0, or its predecessor when x is below
# x0, that is when x1 < 0.
kernel:        to_down_2
input:         x = x0 x1
output:        t
value:         x
requires:      canonical x
ensures:       rounded t down
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/Convert.v to_down_2_correct
source:        the sign of x1 (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   proved
ieee_theorem:  proofs/theories/IeeeExt.v to_down_2_ieee_correct
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   t is x0 or pred(x0), chosen by select, and pred(+inf) is finite; the non-finite layer tests x0 itself

m = lt(x1, 0)
p = pred(x0)
t = select(m, p, x0)
